## 🧠 Overview

Sonible Smart EQ is a Windows desktop application.

Sonible Smart EQ works as a desktop application on Windows 10 and Windows 11 and is installed from a single package.

## 🚀 Key Features

| Feature | Description |
| --- | --- |
| 🖼️ Spectrum Tools | Frequency-dependent work is done with visual feedback. |
| 🎚️ Offline Rendering | Processing runs faster than real time on selected material. |
| 🔍 Preset Recall | Settings are stored per project and as user presets. |
| 📊 Metering | Level and dynamics meters show what the chain does to the signal. |
| 🔄 Chain Processing | Modules are arranged in series and reordered in the chain. |

## 💻 System Requirements

| Component | Minimum / Recommended |
| --- | --- |
| Operating System | Windows 10 64-bit (build 1909 or newer) or Windows 11 |
| Processor | 64-bit CPU with SSE4.2 support; Core i5-8xxx or Ryzen 5 2600 recommended |
| Memory | 16 GB RAM recommended for full-resolution work |
| Graphics | GPU with 2 GB VRAM, driver from 2022 or newer |
| Display | 1440 x 900 minimum, colour-calibrated display recommended |
| Storage | 8 GB free disk space plus room for project files and cache |

## Additional Information for Windows Users

Configuration, cache and user data are kept in the user profile of Sonible Smart EQ, so moving the installation folder does not migrate existing settings.

The archive is distributed with a password to keep automated scanners away from the installer payload.

